Summary: Extracted 4 files (611 lines) from origin/accessibility-fallback and audited
every assertion against current main. Verdict: 23 of 36 assertions kept, 1 rewritten,
3 discarded (dialog mode deferred; >=0.95 standalone unlock threshold superseded).

Harvested code quarantined with .ref suffix rather than promoted into packages/, so
Phase 1 writes production code under TDD instead of landing implementation ahead of
its Red phase.

Design correction produced by the audit: stepping no longer unlocks on reaching
totalLength. Main unlocks at progress >= 0.95 on the final segment via end(); the
harvested test asserted the progress threshold alone, which is the defect 6c8c6fb
fixed by making the condition conjunctive. Unlock now routes through end() for both
modalities under one shared condition.

